.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt DEVD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm devd
.Nd device manager: match pci: devices and launch drivers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/devd
.Nm /sbin/devd
.Ar test
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the driver table from
.Pa /etc/drivers.toml
inside the initfs archive, reads the device directory from the
.Dq pci:
scheme, and matches each device by vendor and device id.  For a match it opens
the BAR selected by the driver's
.Va bar
argument (default
.Ql 0 )
and one page of the function's PCI configuration space, then spawns the
configured driver in a new process.  Both
.Dv MmioRegion
handles are transferred into the child before its first thread starts, in
order: the BAR is the child's handle 3 and the configuration page its handle 4
(a fresh child has 0 for itself, 1 for the initfs and 2 for the namespace).  The
child does not receive the RootDevice capability.
.Pp
When the driver's arguments contain
.Ql resources=dma+irq ,
.Nm
also opens
.Pa /dma
and
.Pa /irq
for the same function.  The 64 KiB DMA buffer is handle 5 and the legacy IRQ
handle 6.  If the list names only one resource, only that handle is added, in
the same order; the endpoint exists on every 3.0 function, but a function that
reports interrupt line 255 has no IRQ.  This is how a driver gets the memory and
interrupt a queue needs while still receiving no RootDevice and no
.Dv ADMIN .
.Pp
Before the spawn,
.Nm
reads
.Pa /bars
for the chosen index, refuses an I/O or absent BAR, and appends four arguments
to the driver's own:
.Ql bar= Ns Ar n ,
.Ql bar_size= Ns Ar bytes ,
and, when requested,
.Ql dma= Ns Ar len
and
.Ql irq= Ns Ar line ,
so a driver never guesses the regions or the line it was given.
.Nm
keeps its own copy of every handle it opened and closes all of them after the
driver exits, so a crash and restart cannot leak a DMA buffer or a claimed IRQ
line.
.Pp
The driver table is a small
.Ql [[driver]]
TOML subset:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[[driver]]
name = "dummy"
vendor = 0x1234
device = 0x11e8
exec = "/sbin/devd"
args = ["bar=0", "resources=dma+irq"]
cycles = 10
.Ed
.Pp
.Va name
and
.Va exec
are required;
.Va args
defaults to an empty list and
.Va cycles
defaults to 1 with a maximum of 100.  An argument of the form
.Ql bar= Ns Ar n
is consumed by
.Nm
as the BAR selector (never passed to the child); the form
.Ql resources= Ns Ar list
requests resources, with
.Ql dma+irq
and
.Ql none
as the accepted values (a
.Ql +
rather than a comma, because the table parser splits an array on commas).  A
malformed table or an executable path that does not start with
.Pa /
is rejected before any spawn.
.Pp
Without arguments
.Nm
launches the matched driver once and then registers the
.Dq dev:
scheme.  With
.Ar test
it launches the driver for the manifest's
.Va cycles
count, prints one
.Dq devd: driver Ar name Dq cycle N exit=C
line per cycle, reaps every child, closes every resource handle and exits with
status 0.  This is the lifecycle path exercised by the
.Ql devd
qtest.
.Pp
The
.Ql dummy
argument is the built-in test driver.  It maps the transferred BAR, verifies
that
.Dv MMIO_CREATE
on that non-root handle fails with
.Er EPERM ,
and exits 0.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/devd.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/drivers.toml
driver match table
.It Pa /etc/services.d/devd.toml
service manifest
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pcid 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr svcd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
server first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
